            <description><![CDATA[<!-- What Sparkle's update dialog shows for 1.3.0. generate_appcast embeds any
     Belay-<version>.html it finds beside the matching DMG; publish-appcast.sh
     copies these files there. One file per version, English only: Sparkle's
     dialog has no locale negotiation, and half-translated notes read worse
     than plainly-written English ones. -->
<style>
  body { font: 13px -apple-system, sans-serif; color: #333; margin: 12px 16px; }
  h2 { font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 8px; }
  ul { padding-left: 20px; margin: 6px 0; }
  li { margin-bottom: 6px; }
  p.quiet { color: #777; margin: 8px 0 0; }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    body { color: #ddd; } p.quiet { color: #999; }
  }
</style>
<h2>Belay 1.3</h2>
<ul>
  <li><b>The display dims at night.</b> Step away and it fades to a glow;
      come back and it brightens. Off by default, in
      Settings&nbsp;&#9656;&nbsp;Behavior.</li>
  <li><b>The lid can close now.</b> An optional helper keeps the run alive
      with the lid shut, and always lets go by itself: at the time limit, or
      if the Mac gets too warm.</li>
  <li><b>Held through the retries.</b> An agent waiting out an overloaded
      model no longer reads as idle. Belay keeps holding.</li>
</ul>
<p class="quiet">Also: small sounds for the welcome and What&#8217;s New
screens, and a fuller local log. Nothing leaves your Mac, as ever.</p>
]]></description>
